==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|anadiplosis}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|ἀναδίπλωσις}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|anadiploses}}

# {{context|rhetoric|lang=en}} A [[rhetoric]]al device in which a word or phrase used at the end of a sentence or clause is repeated near the beginning of the next sentence or clause.
{{examples-right|examples="Suffering produces endurance, and endurance produces character, and character produces hope." (Romans 5:3-4)}}

